Inherited/adapted upstream files (paths relative to upstream root):
- src/cvio_asl_ldam/losses/asl_ldam.py
  Ported to losses.py; preserves formulas and default parameters. Verified
  float32 values and gradients against upstream numerical fixtures.
- src/cvio_asl_ldam/attention/simam_dcfr.py
  Ported to attention.py; preserves SimAM, texture, gate and residual operations.
  Verified output, input gradient and every parameter gradient against upstream.
- src/cvio_asl_ldam/attention/patch_yolo.py
  Adapted in trainer.py for Ultralytics 8.4.72. Corrects evaluation tuple to use
  logits, wires all configured loss parameters, verifies pretrained transfer
  before wrapping the classifier, probes actual input channels, preserves the
  complete custom model on resume, and audits restored optimizer/EMA state.
- src/cvio_asl_ldam/models/yolo_train.py
  Orchestration reimplemented in ../cvio_run.py: immutable run identity, explicit
  paths, full membership/hash verification, byte-preserving train/val staging,
  no test staging, guarded completion/skip/resume, evaluation and evidence ZIPs.
- src/cvio_asl_ldam/utils/run_guard.py
  Reference for lifecycle semantics; corrected completion-status cycle. No
  assertion that a directory or a running status proves a completed experiment.
- configs/train/yolo26m_ce.yaml
- configs/train/yolo26m_asl_ldam_simam_dcfr.yaml
  Frozen recipe values in ../configs and validated by config.py. Checkpoint
  selection remains native Ultralytics classification fitness. final_eval no
  longer strips optimizer state; best-checkpoint validation is explicit.

New integration support: runtime.py configures a local settings directory,
disables third-party tracking, and requires the qualified Ultralytics version.
It restores native Pillow Image.open after the runtime's global HEIF patch,
keeping PNG/JPEG decode and corrupt-input error behavior isolated from training.
../cvio_run.py and ../../scripts/run_cvio_kaggle.py record actual runtime,
configuration and checksums. These additions do not assert bitwise reproduction
of the unavailable official SDI-4 training environment or published scores.

